                <pb facs="0756" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/887: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-21T13:00:00+08:00">November 21, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>168. Embassy’s 160, November 19, 5 p.m.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d628-f1"/>
                    Following from Yunnanfu: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 20, 4 p.m. Referring to the Embassy’s telegram November 9, 11
                            a.m. to Canton.</p>
                        <p>Yunnan having its own monetary system independent of the Central
                            Government, this province is not affected by the nationalization of
                            silver and there has been little comment engendered thereby. Yunnan
                            silver currency continues to circulate”.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
